{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01HpT56dqnRBBQ1nU7XzM8rV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I notice several issues. Let me trace through the data more carefully:\n\n1. T002 is on 2024-03-02 which is AFTER biz_date 2024-03-01 - correct\n2. T003 is on 2024-02-28 (before biz_date) but status PENDING - that's correct\n3. T004 duplicate - but the first T004 at row 4 should be valid (it's on 2024-02-15, POSTED, for A1002)\n\nWait, let me re-check the transactions file. Row 5 and 6 both have T004. Row 5 is the first, row 6 is DUPLICATE. But my output says row 5 is DUPLICATE. The row_num should be 1-based data row (after header), so:\n- Row 1: T001\n- Row 2: T002\n- Row 3: T003\n- Row 4: T004 (first)\n- Row 5: T004 (duplicate)\n\nSo row 5 T004 DUPLICATE is correct.\n\nLet me also check the reversal logic - T005 and T006 should both be REVERSED because T006 has reversal_of=T005.\n\nLooking at T009 and T010: T010 has reversal_of=T009, so both should be REVERSED. That's correct.\n\nT017 has reversal_of=T018, and T018 exists in file, so both should be REVERSED. That's correct.\n\nBut wait - T008 has reversal_of=NOPE which is NOT in the file, so it should be REVERSAL_MISSING. That's correct.\n\nNow let me check A1002 balance. Let me trace through:\n- Start: 5000.00\n- T004 (row 4): +50.00 USD, PLAN_B applies to ALL\n  - Fee = 0.10 + 0.002 * 50 = 0.10 + 0.10 = 0.20, capped to [0.10, 2.00] = 0.20\n  - adjusted = 50.00 - 0.20 = 49.80\n- T011 (row 12): +5.00 USD\n  - Fee = 0.10 + 0.002 * 5 = 0.10 + 0.01 = 0.11\n  - adjusted = 5.00 - 0.11 = 4.89\n- T015 (row 16): +100.00 CAD -> USD\n\nFor T015: CAD -> USD on 2024-03-01\n- Direct CAD->USD? No\n- Reverse USD->CAD? No\n- Pivot GBP: CAD->GBP? Yes (2024-02-01: CAD->GBP 0.5800), GBP->USD?\n  - Direct GBP->USD? No. Reverse USD->GBP? Yes (2024-03-01: USD->GBP 0.8000)\n  - Rate = 1/0.8000 = 1.25\n  - Pivot rate = 0.58 * 1.25 = 0.725\n  - 100 CAD * 0.725 = 72.50 USD\n\nWait, let me recheck. I think T002 is on 2024-03-02 but looking at my code, T002 at row 2 has effective_date 2024-03-02 which is after biz_date 2024-03-01. So that's AFTER_BIZ_DATE. But T002 at row 2 is also the same row - let me re-check the order of checks.\n\nLet me trace through T002 (row 2):\n- REVERSED? T002 is not in reversedTxIds (no reversal_of points to T002), and row 2 is not in reversalRows. Not reversed.\n- REVERSAL_MISSING? reversalOf is empty. No.\n- FX_MISSING? Account A1001 is USD, tx currency is EUR. Need FX EUR->USD on 2024-03-02. But wait, my code checks FX before AFTER_BIZ_DATE!\n\nThe order in the requirements says:\n1. REVERSED\n2. REVERSAL_MISSING\n3. FX_MISSING (before FX)\n4. AFTER_BIZ_DATE\n5. status!=POSTED\n6. DUPLICATE\n\nSo the order is FX_MISSING before AFTER_BIZ_DATE. My current code does that. But T002 is dated 2024-03-02. Let me check if there's EUR->USD rate for that date:\n- EUR->USD direct: 2024-03-01 rate 1.0870 (latest <= 2024-03-02)\n- So FX exists.\n\nSo T002 should be AFTER_BIZ_DATE. That's correct in my output.\n\nLet me verify A1001 balance:\n- Start: 10000.00\n- T001 (row 1): -2000.00 USD, PLAN_A applies to DEBIT only\n  - This is a debit (negative), so fee applies\n  - Fee = 0.50 + 0.005 * 2000 = 0.50 + 10 = 10.50, capped to max 5.00\n  - adjusted = -2000.00 - 5.00 = -2005.00\n- T013 (row 14): +30.00 GBP on 2024-02-10 -> USD\n  - GBP->USD on 2024-02-10: Direct? No. Reverse USD->GBP? Yes, 2024-02-01: 0.7900\n  - Rate = 1/0.7900 = 1.2658227848... (10dp)\n  - 30 * 1.2658227848 = 37.974683544... -> 37.97 (2dp after FX)\n  - Wait, the FX conversion should be 10dp intermediate. Let me check my code.\n  - Credit, PLAN_A only applies to DEBIT, so no fee\n  - adjusted = 37.9746835443 -> 37.97 (2dp)\n- T014 (row 15): -10000.00 JPY on 2024-03-01 -> USD\n  - JPY->USD on 2024-03-01: Direct JPY->USD? Check... 2024-02-01 has JPY->USD 0.0067\n  - That's the latest <= 2024-03-01\n  - But wait, USD->JPY 150.00 is on 2024-03-01. So we need to compare dates.\n  - Direct JPY->USD: 2024-02-01 at 0.0067\n  - Reverse (USD->JPY then invert): 2024-03-01 at 150.00, inverted = 1/150 = 0.0066666667\n  - Reverse date 2024-03-01 > Direct date 2024-02-01, so use reverse rate\n  - Rate = 0.0066666667\n  - -10000 * 0.0066666667 = -66.66666667 USD\n  - This is a debit, PLAN_A applies\n  - Fee = 0.50 + 0.005 * 66.67 = 0.50 + 0.3333 = 0.8333... -> 0.83 (2dp HALF_EVEN)\n  - But capped to [0.25, 5.00], so 0.83\n  - adjusted = -66.67 - 0.83 = -67.50 (rounded)\n  \nWait, I need to check my FX conversion more carefully. Let me re-read my code:\n\n```java\nBigDecimal amountInAcctCcy = tx.amount;\nif (!tx.currency.equals(acct.currency)) {\n    BigDecimal rate = findFxRate(tx.currency, acct.currency, tx.effectiveDate, fxRates, pivots);\n    amountInAcctCcy = tx.amount.multiply(rate).setScale(10, RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN);\n}\n```\n\nSo I multiply by rate and keep 10dp. Then when applying fee, I do setScale(2). Let me trace through again.\n\nT014: -10000.00 JPY -> USD\n- Rate JPY->USD = 0.0066666667 (1/150 rounded to 10dp)\n- amountInAcctCcy = -10000 * 0.0066666667 = -66.6666666700 (10dp)\n- Fee applies (DEBIT, PLAN_A)\n- Fee = 0.50 + 0.005 * 66.6666666700 = 0.50 + 0.3333333334 = 0.8333333334\n- Fee rounded 2dp = 0.83\n- Fee capped to [0.25, 5.00] = 0.83\n- adjusted = -66.6666666700 - 0.83 = -67.4966666700 -> -67.50 (2dp HALF_EVEN)\n\nT016 duplicate at row 18: T016 first appears at row 17 for A9999 (non-existent account). But since A9999 doesn't exist, we skip it silently. Then row 18 T016 for A1001 - is this DUPLICATE? Yes, because we've seen T016 before even though the first one was skipped silently.\n\nHmm wait, let me check my logic again. Looking at my code:\n\n```java\n// Account not found (silent skip, not exception)\nif (reason == null && acct == null) {\n    skippedTxs++;\n    seenTxIds.add(tx.txId);\n    continue;\n}\n```\n\nSo for row 17 (T016, A9999), we skip silently AND add T016 to seenTxIds. Then row 18 (T0